PRISM: warp backdrop, borderless material, kit type, kit shadows

The backdrop is a warped perspective grid with spectrum beams, in CSS and
motion, and the same effect in both themes.

It is the third attempt and the first that works in light mode. VANTA.HALO
could not: its ring is additive light, so on a near-white ground every
channel is already near 255 and it clips to white. Measured on one clip of
one page, dark came back at 0.308 saturation over 593 distinct colours and
light at 0.015 over ONE. A WebGL tubes effect fixed that (geometry paints
rather than adds) but followed a cursor, and our creators are on phones.
This paints, needs no pointer, and costs no WebGL context at all: three,
vanta and the 757KB threejs-components build are all gone and nothing
replaced them, because motion was already a dependency.

The published snippet could not ship as written. It used motion.div, which
THROWS here under LazyMotion strict; it picked every beam colour with
Math.random() during render, so the background was random colour and
reshuffled on every re-render; it defaulted to a shadcn token we do not
have; and it was a wrapper with border and padding rather than a backdrop.
Measured after: zero horizontal overflow and zero console errors at 375,
768, 1024 and 1440, in both themes.

Borders are gone from the material, per Rashid: the neo utilities no
longer draw a hairline, and nor do buttons, inputs, both toggles or the
menu button. The one place a border survives is forced-colors, where
Windows High Contrast discards box-shadow outright and a shadow-only
control is not subtle but invisible.

Shadows now follow the kit, which specifies them: Ink-tinted rather than
the cool blue-grey that was there, and roughly 2:1 blur to offset rather
than 1:2, which is what made surfaces read as outlined even before the
hairline counted.

Typography is the kit's: Caprasimo and Figtree, self-hosted, Sora dropped,
net about +16KB. Sizes converted from the kit's px to rem so they still
follow the text-size control.

Also: the light accent gradient hovered to #74501a -> #8f6624, so the
primary button turned GOLD on hover in light mode, the twin of the dark
bug fixed earlier and missed because only the dark pair was checked. The
admin Categorise button painted --wx-on-accent on --wx-surface-3, which is
white on near-white in light and #14141c on #14141c in dark: invisible in
both. Dark surfaces move off the purple at Rashid's request. Buttons are
pills at every size, per the kit, instead of four different radii. The tab
icon is the kit's square 512 tile rather than the 40x96 "i", which was a
sliver at 16px, and tiktok-app-icon is re-rendered from the white tile.

Not verified: every signed-in screen. There is no creator login on dev and
no service key or admin credentials here, so nothing behind the login can
be opened. The login page is measured in both themes at four widths.
